<title>SINGAPORE: Low Keng Huat first half loss deepens.</title>
<headline>Low Keng Huat first half loss deepens.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			(2.43)    vs     (0.24)</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	 (2.03)    vs     (0.19)</p>
<p>    Turnover			32.79     vs     31.37</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     1.10     vs	2.22</p>
<p>    Interest expense	    (3.30)    vs     (2.34)</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation (2.32)    vs     (0.92)</p>
<p>    Investment/other income    0.62     vs	0.82</p>
<p>    Profits from associates    1.61     vs	1.09</p>
<p>    Tax				0.69     vs	0.40</p>
<p>    Minorities	(gain)     1.17     vs	0.11</p>
<p>Note - Low Keng Huat Ltd said losses were due mainly to start-up costs of its Saigon Prince Hotel and lower construction volume and margins.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
